---

# Constitutional Invariants

Every Executive Decision:

- References one or more Recommendations.
- Belongs to one Organization.
- Belongs to one Assessment.
- Has an accountable decision-maker.
- Creates organizational commitment.
- Cannot exist without Recommendations.

---

# Relationship to Accountability

Accountability begins at the Decision.

Reality creates Observations.

Observations create Evidence.

Evidence produces Findings.

Findings produce Recommendations.

Only Executive Decisions create organizational accountability.

---

# Relationship to Trust

FLUANZ never replaces executive judgment.

Its purpose is to maximize decision quality by ensuring every Decision is supported by complete traceability.

Observation

↓

Evidence

↓

Finding

↓

Recommendation

↓

Executive Decision

Trust culminates in accountable human choice.

---

# Architectural Discovery

Executive Decisions represent the transition from business understanding to organizational commitment.

This is the final responsibility of the Organization.

No AI system can own this responsibility.

No automation engine can inherit this accountability.

The Organization alone decides.

---

# Constitutional Laws

## Constitutional Law 09.1

Executive Decisions are derived from Recommendations.

---

## Constitutional Law 09.2

Only authorized decision-makers may create Executive Decisions.

---

## Constitutional Law 09.3

Executive Decisions establish organizational accountability.

---

## Constitutional Law 09.4

FLUANZ informs decisions but never replaces them.

---

## Constitutional Law 09.5

Accountability begins at the moment an Executive Decision is made.

---

# Open Questions

- Can one Executive Decision approve multiple Recommendations?
- Can Recommendations be partially approved?
- Can Executive Decisions be reversed?
- Should rationale be part of the Decision?
- Should expected business outcomes be recorded?
- How should historical Decisions influence future Assessments?

---

# Workshop Outcome

Executive Decisions complete the advisory lifecycle of FLUANZ.

Observations establish facts.

Evidence establishes proof.

Findings establish understanding.

Recommendations establish guidance.

Executive Decisions establish organizational commitment.

The platform exists to improve the quality of Executive Decisions—not to replace them.

